course: dictionary
lesson: 6137
title: Mildly and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «mildly» makes things softer and weaker. «Mildly interesting» means a little interesting, and «mildly spicy» means a little spicy, not very hot. When you meet mildly, ask yourself: is the thing a bit less strong than I thought?
explain: Mildly can also mean gentle and calm. If someone speaks mildly, their voice is soft and their words are not sharp. The words around the word give you the clue: a person who speaks mildly is not shouting or getting cross.
explain: Watch out for «to put it mildly». This phrase is a trick: it means the truth is even stronger than the words. «The test was hard, to put it mildly» means the test was far harder than the word hard suggests. You can check with your swap test: does «a little hard» fit? It does not, because the phrase says the opposite.
explain: Words from other places can use mildly too. A Russian friend might say, «"tormoz", literally "brake", means a slowcoach, someone slow to get a joke; it is mildly mean but fine between pals». So the word for slow is a little unkind, but friends can laugh at it together. Context helps you see how strong a word is.
fact: Mildly means slightly, or in a gentle, calm way.
fact: «Mildly interesting» means a little interesting, not very interesting.
fact: «To put it mildly» means the truth is even stronger than your words: «The test was hard, to put it mildly» means it was much harder.
fact: In science, «mildly acidic» means a little acidic.
fact: Regional words: «tormoz» (Russian slang) literally means brake, and means a slowcoach, someone slow to get a joke.
exercise: «The film was mildly scary, so the little ones giggled.» What does mildly mean here? | *A little, not very much | Extremely, to the max | Backwards | Hardly ever
exercise: «She spoke mildly, so nobody felt shouted at.» What does mildly suggest about how she spoke? | She spoke very fast | She was telling a silly joke | She was shouting very loudly | *Her voice was calm and gentle
exercise: Ruby says, «The test was hard, to put it mildly.» What does this phrase suggest? | The test was easy | The test was cancelled | *The test was even harder than the words say | The test was a little bit hard
test: «The soup was mildly spicy.» What does this mean? | *A little spicy, not very hot | Extremely spicy and burning | Cold and sour | Sweet like sugar
test: Tom says, «The race was tiring, to put it mildly.» Why does he say mildly? | The race was a little tiring, exactly as he says | The race was not tiring at all | Tom was calm about the race | *The race was much more tiring than he says
exam: Which phrase means the truth is even stronger than the words? | Mildly acidic | Mildly spicy | *To put it mildly | Mildly interesting
